`verilator_config
// scoped per-line and individually justified against the V0 triage
// (verif/v0/kve/RESULT.md §6). kvq_engine.sv and every TB in this directory
// are -Wall clean with NO waivers. Line numbers are for the vendored copies
// (upstream + 9/16/18-line provenance headers).

// ── cq_units_syn.sv (V0 §6: every WIDTH site individually triaged benign) ───
// dequant/scale/quant fp16 cores: sign-extended adds/compares (lossless) and
// two masked truncations ((Q>>sh)&mask keeps only in-range bits). The quant
// clamp COND (l.299) selects between two values both provably <= 127 post-
// clamp; proven bit-exact vs golden across all 9 vector sets.
// (Line numbers re-based 2026-07-08 for the D-020 header + `clear` additions
//  in the vendored copies — SAME waivers on the SAME constructs, nothing new
//  waived; the D-020 clear logic itself is warning-free.)
// unused high/sign bits of unpack intermediates (mantissa fields consumed
// piecewise); cq_quant_comb is dead in this hierarchy by design
// upstream keeps the four cq cores in one file (P4b layout)

// ── amax_unit.sv ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// l.107-109: `nm` blocking scratch inside the sequential block is DELIBERATE
// (yosys mem2reg workaround, documented in the file); l.35: fp16 sign bits of
// `vec` are intentionally not consumed (magnitude compare clears them).

// ── cq_key_path.sv ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// upstream style: unused counter top bits (l.122 rb_fill / l.133 ch,sch guard
// bits) and int-vs-sized compares in the FSM (l.247/262/273), all lossless;
// scale_token deliberately unconnected in key mode (l.141)
// (re-based 2026-07-08 for the D-020 clear/busy additions — same constructs)

